a long-awaited report into child sexual  abuse in football has found significant  institutional failings on the part of  the football association  and says the sports governing body put  children at risk  over a five-year period the sheldon  review was commissioned  in 2016 after several men waived their  right to anonymity to speak  about their experiences well one of the  most prolific offenders was the football  coach and convicted  pedophile barry bonnell the report found  that during his time at manchester city  senior management at the club were made  aware of rumors but didn't  investigate it adds that some members of  staff appear to have referred to him as  a kitty fiddler  it also concluded that abusers used the  colog the cloak of respectability to win  over boys and their parents and that the  men were manipulative  and used elaborate grooming practices  in later years between 1995 and 2000 the  review says the fa acted far  too slowly to introduce effective child  protection measures and that there were  significant institutional failings for  which there is no excuse  and i found that up until august 2020  there were 240  suspects of sexual abuse and at least  692 survivors  well our sports correspondent martha  kellner joins us live from  crew it's pretty damning isn't it martha  it certainly is as you mentioned there  survivors have waited an  awfully long time for the release of  this report  it was commissioned four years ago back  in 2016  when andy woodward became the first  footballer to wave his right to  anonymity  and reveal that he had suffered abuse by  barry bonnell that prolific  football sex abuser that we all now know  so much  about and now it has finally arrived  this report it's 707 pages long  it's exhaustive in its detail and it's  damning in its verdict particularly for  the football association while the  report  finds no evidence of a conspiracy or  collusion to cover up  within the football association it does  find that over a five-year period  between october 2000 and sorry i'll just  get those  dates for you between um october  1995 and may 2000 that five year period  that they consistently let down children  within  football clive sheldon qc the barrister  who authored the report wrote  the fa should have engaged more deeply  with the issue of child protection and  should have acted more quickly to bring  in comprehensive measures  to safeguard children in the game these  are significant  institutional failings for which there  is no  excuse now the report spoke to 62  survivors and  157 other individuals  it focuses on seven abusers barry  bonnell who was also  a football scout and coach here at crew  alexandra  also at manchester city but it also  focuses on six  other abusers the report identifies  historical  failings at several football clubs they  are chelsea  aston villa newcastle manchester city  crew alexandra where i am  stoke peterborough and southampton  now some survivors did provide testimony  to  to clive sheldon qc stating that they  believed  there was a pedophile ring within  football  clive sheldon accepted that some of  these perpetrators  may have known each other but he didn't  think that they acted together to abuse  young boys that is one of the key  findings of this report  some survivors also want to see  mandatory reporting  that would be a legal requirement for  those who know that abuse is going on  to report it to a higher authority clive  sheldon  qc said that was not within his remit  and now he did however  recommend 13 recommendations including  the publishing of a safeguarding report  every year and also an annual  safeguarding in football  day but clearly this is going to be a  highly emotional day  for the survivors of that abuse we may  call it historical abuse  but it's still very much having a  physical and psychological effect  on those survivors right up until the  present day  as you can see from an interview i did  earlier today um with david  lean who was a victim of barry bonnell  that's it it impacts you sort of every  day  it doesn't go away and you know i've  said this many times i can close my eyes  and put myself back into that room  it's that easy to do that you know and  so  um i wasn't three four five year old i  was 12  and you know i was at high school i've  got very vivid memories of exactly what  happened  um so yeah we live with it every day  people don't realise how  big an effect it takes on your whole  your whole family  yeah i wasn't um i wasn't  sort of planning on getting you know  emotional today i've spoke about it a  lot  um but yeah  it does  hugely emotional there from david lean  now one of the clubs which the report  focuses on is crew alexandra  where barry bernell spent many years and  committed  many offences against many young boys  the report finds that while there was no  obvious cover-up at crew alexandra  there were persistent rumors that barry  bonnell had a sexual  interest in children rumors which the  report concludes that some  coaches would probably have heard about  now dario grady was director of football  here up until 2019  he was also here at the time of barry  bernell's offending  um and we tried um to get a word with  with dario grady earlier  hello sir hi how are you  i'm  i'm under instructions sorry is there  any comment you'd like to make to the  victims  they've just said no sorry  bye  dario grady they're very reluctant to  comment but we do expect to hear from  the football association  later on today you would expect given  how damning the verdict is of this  report given  findings of institutional failings  within that organization  that five years which they were found to  have put to  put children playing football around the  country at risk  that it will force that organization the  national governing body for football  in this country into an apology an  apology that victims have waited an  awful long time for
 

